version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-09-15"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/officialarghya29/dinov2-lowlight-robustness"
keywords:
  - self-supervised learning
  - DINOv2
  - vision transformers
  - robustness
  - low-light
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - CKA
abstract: >-
  A controlled study localizing where a frozen DINOv2 ViT fails under a
  physically motivated low-light ladder: the ADC is innocent, drift compounds
  through depth (replicating and steepening on ViT-B/14), the fixed readout
  collapses to a constant class set by embedding geometry rather than the
  training prior, and readout-side repair beats every input-space
  enhancement and sensor-side fix. Full harness, statistical machinery with
  unit tests, and committed artifacts for every number.
